Falcon round-3 known-answer-test values
=======================================

Source: the file `falcon512-KAT.rsp` of the Falcon round-3 submission package (specification v1.2), by the Falcon
Project, as posted by NIST and on falcon-sign.info:

  https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/post-quantum-cryptography/documents/round-3/submissions/Falcon-Round3.zip
  https://falcon-sign.info/falcon-round3.zip

`falcon512-KAT.rsp` (1250115 bytes, 100 entries) has sha256
dd75c946fdedef4ec46a2bee7e10c65c9126f1a839b9ced6921fd45f7354b5cd in both archives. The file itself is not in this
repository; evidence/README.md says where to download it.

Files of this repository that contain values from it:

- FalconPrecision/Exec/WitnessData.lean: `sk` of entries 0 and 70, as hexadecimal strings copied from the file, and
  values computed from entries 0 and 70.
- test/ExecRound3.lean: `sk` and `pk` of entry 0, as hexadecimal strings copied from the file.
- test/ExecCodec.lean: `msg` and `sm` of entry 0, and the salt and message bytes of `sm` of entry 70, as
  hexadecimal strings copied from the file, and a value computed from entry 0.
- evidence/vectors/d45/e0.json, evidence/vectors/d45/e70.json, evidence/vectors/d45/e27.json,
  evidence/vectors/d127/e0.json, evidence/vectors/d127/e70.json: the polynomials f, g, F, G decoded from `sk` and
  s2 decoded from `sm` of entries 0, 70 and 27, and values computed from these entries.

The run files that scripts/gen_evidence_runs.py writes to `runs/` contain values of all 100 entries; they are
written from the reader's own copy of the file and are not part of this repository.

Falcon specification test vectors
=================================

test/ExecSampler.lean contains the 16 SamplerZ test vectors of Table 3.2 (p. 44) of the Falcon specification v1.2
(round 3), part of the same submission package, copied from the specification.

